summary:
  The sync engine undoes a park when a Bluetooth speaker leaves the group.

history:
  This is the exception that was taken out on 2026-09-21. A speaker powering
  off says goodbye with an AVRCP pause, and with other speakers still in the
  room that pause was treated as the speaker's: a park up to two minutes old
  was resumed when the member left. It could not tell a speaker from a
  person — a keyboard's media key arrives over MPRIS too — and on the desk a
  pause sent over MPRIS was undone five seconds after the speaker's link
  dropped. "Left the group" also fires when nothing left (a profile switch
  recreated the node the same morning), so a pause and a hiccup a minute
  later was enough. The engine measures and routes; it has no road to sound.
  This number used to guard the origin mark that exception depended on.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
              _btJoinWatchArm(known, lastName);
          }
      }

replace:
              _btJoinWatchArm(known, lastName); if (app.timeshiftResume) app.timeshiftResume();
          }
      }

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_pause_is_a_pause_whoever_leaves_the_room.
  Line-neutral.
